Advantech MIC-733-AO: MB1 boot pinmux and boot GPIO configuration.

Creates tegra234-mb1-bct-gpio-p3701-0000-a04-mic-733-ao.dtsi and
tegra234-mb1-bct-pinmux-p3701-0000-a04-mic-733-ao.dtsi from NVIDIA R39.2.1's
tegra234-mb1-bct-{gpio,pinmux}-p3701-0000-a04.dtsi. flash-qspi.sh copies the
two NVIDIA files to these names (sha256-checked) and applies this patch to the
copies with `patch -p1` from the root of Linux_for_Tegra; NVIDIA's own files
are not modified. mic-733-ao-qspi.conf selects the copies.

Source of the changes: Advantech's r36.4.x MB1 files for the MIC-733-AO as
published by Avocado Linux (avocado-linux/bsp-mic-733-ao5a1,
stone/carrier-bsp/tegra234-mb1-bct-{pinmux,gpio}-p3701-0000-a04-adv.dtsi).
Compared semantically (per pin, per property; comments ignored) against
NVIDIA's stock r36.4.3 files, Advantech changes exactly these pins, and
NVIDIA R39.2.1 has the r36.4.3 values for all of them (usb_vbus_en1_pz2:
R39.2.1 already pulls up, like Advantech). Only the changed values are applied;
NVIDIA's own r36 -> r39 changes (dp_aux_ch1/2/3 and soc_gpio38/40/55 moved
from the eth functions to rsvd1) are kept as NVIDIA has them.

  pinmux  dp_aux_ch0_hpd_pm0     dp -> rsvd1 (GPIO M.00, HDMI hot-plug)
          pex_l0_clkreq_n_pk0    rsvd1 -> pe0, un-tristated (PCIe C0)
          pex_l0_rst_n_pk1       rsvd1 -> pe0, un-tristated, input off
          pex_l7_clkreq_n_pag0   rsvd1 -> pe7, un-tristated (PCIe C7)
          pex_l7_rst_n_pag1      rsvd1 -> pe7, un-tristated, input off
          soc_gpio23_pp4         pull down -> up (TPM present, active low)
          soc_gpio31_pq4         input enabled, pull none -> down
          spi1_sck/miso/mosi/cs0/cs1 (pz3-pz7)  rsvd1 -> spi1, un-tristated,
                                 pull up (sck stays pull down), lpdr dropped
          spi5_mosi_pac2         input enabled
          usb_vbus_en0_pz1       driven (un-tristated, input off, 1.8 V)
          usb_vbus_en1_pz2       driven (un-tristated, input off)
  gpio    inputs added           M.00 M.03 M.05 M.06 Q.04 AC.02
          output-high            Z.01 Z.02 N.01 (were inputs)
          output-low             AON BB.00 (was input); AC.02 removed
          Q.04 stays in output-low as well: Advantech lists it in both.

Not changed: pad voltage (Advantech's file is byte-identical to NVIDIA
r36.4.3; NVIDIA R39.2.1 differs only in whitespace and header), UPHY lanes.

Licence: these are NVIDIA BSD-3-Clause files; the NVIDIA notice is retained.
Avocado publishes Advantech's versions without a LICENSE file; only the pin
values above, which are hardware facts of the carrier, are taken from them.

